            <ArticleTitle>Two-Photon Luminescence and Second-Harmonic Generation in Organic Nonlinear Surface Comprised of Self-Assembled Frustum Shaped Organic Microlasers.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/adma.201605260</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An ultrathin nonlinear optical (NLO) organic surface composed of numerous self-assembled frustum-shaped whispering-gallery-mode resonators displays both two-photon luminescence and second-harmonic-generation signals. A super-second-order increase of the NLO intensity with respect to pump power confirms the microlasing action and practical usefulness of the NLO organic surfaces.</AbstractText>
